(5202527, 753820, 68947, '<td valign="top">I like the lighting and composition of this shot.  It''s really well done and the border adds a lot to the shot as well.  <br/> <br/>You know, it''s ironic that we went through a huge discussion on "artwork" in a photo and what categorized a shot that is chiefly a shot of a piece of artwork.  Throughout that discussion, it was debated as to what could be defined as a shot of a piece of "artwork" and what was acceptable within that realm.  This is clearly a shot (very well done) of a piece of artwork as it is man-made/a replica.  Yet, it placed 4th in the rankings.  <br/> <br/>Clearly, if a piece of artwork is well photographed, it will do well.  <br/> <br/>Congrats on your placement and in this shot proving a point that was so very much discussed in-depth, mostly against this type of thing.  It''s proven that it''s all in the way that it is done and not the artwork that''s the issue.  :)</td>', 'I like the lighting and composition of this shot.  It''s really well done and the border adds a lot to the shot as well.   You know, it''s ironic that we went through a huge discussion on "artwork" in a photo and what categorized a shot that is chiefly a shot of a piece of artwork.  Throughout that discussion, it was debated as to what could be defined as a shot of a piece of "artwork" and what was acceptable within that realm.  This is clearly a shot (very well done) of a piece of artwork as it is man-made/a replica.  Yet, it placed 4th in the rankings.   Clearly, if a piece of artwork is well photographed, it will do well.   Congrats on your placement and in this shot proving a point that was so very much discussed in-depth, mostly against this type of thing.  It''s proven that it''s all in the way that it is done and not the artwork that''s the issue.  :)', '2009-01-18 18:37:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(5203688, 753393, 39825, '<td valign="top">:-))) congrats to your ribbon. really very funny. :-) I''m glad you didn''t get it posthumous, but before. :-)))</td>', ':-))) congrats to your ribbon. really very funny. :-) I''m glad you didn''t get it posthumous, but before. :-)))', '2009-01-19 09:01:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(5204101, 753700, 66635, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by HawkeyeLonewolf:</b></div><hr/><i> Great photo, DNMC however. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>How the hell can he say this is DNMC??? WTF?!!</td>', 'Originally posted by HawkeyeLonewolf: Great photo, DNMC however.   How the hell can he say this is DNMC??? WTF?!!', '2009-01-19 11:38:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(5205324, 751728, 73452, '<td valign="top">This is Kari Ann, greetings from the <b>Critique Club:</b> <br/> <br/><b>composition:</b> the leading line of the stripe of metallic draws the eye nicely around the image.<br/> <br/><b>color:</b> a beautiful conversion to black and white<br/> <br/><b>contrast:</b> a little harsh on some of the numbers, but otherwise very interesting<br/> <br/><b>focus:</b> nice and sharp, great focus<br/> <br/><b>depth of field:</b> such a small area, that there isnt that much depth of field. so i cant really say with this one.<br/> <br/><b>lighting: </b> very different, i love how the letters really shine<br/> <br/><b>other: </b> An interesting take on something we view everyday, and never see real beauty in.  great job on capturing the essence of it. I hope you''ll stick around DPC, grow your portfolio, and share more of your work.  If you have any other questions or concerns, feel free to PM me.<br/>-Kari Ann</td>', 'This is Kari Ann, greetings from the Critique Club:  composition: the leading line of the stripe of metallic draws the eye nicely around the image. color: a beautiful conversion to black and white contrast: a little harsh on some of the numbers, but otherwise very interesting focus: nice and sharp, great focus depth of field: such a small area, that there isnt that much depth of field. so i cant really say with this one. lighting:  very different, i love how the letters really shine other:  An interesting take on something we view everyday, and never see real beauty in.  great job on capturing the essence of it. I hope you''ll stick around DPC, grow your portfolio, and share more of your work.  If you have any other questions or concerns, feel free to PM me.-Kari Ann', '2009-01-19 21:06:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(5206305, 753700, 73981, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by OmanOtter:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by HawkeyeLonewolf:</b></div><hr/><i> Great photo, DNMC however. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>How the hell can he say this is DNMC??? WTF?!! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Envy ;)</td>', 'Originally posted by OmanOtter: Originally posted by HawkeyeLonewolf: Great photo, DNMC however.   How the hell can he say this is DNMC??? WTF?!!   Envy ;)', '2009-01-20 07:26:00.000000', NULL, 0),
